# KNITRO options for the fixed-q A middle-loop solver (solve_melitz_fixed_q_A_profile,
# src/melitz/fixed_q_a_middle_loop.jl). Governing-prompt Phase 2's own recommendation:
# "limited-memory or quasi-Newton outer/middle Hessian initially" -- hessopt=6 (L-BFGS)
# rather than the production finite-delta driver's dense BFGS (hessopt=2), since the middle
# problem has up to D^2-1=399 free variables (real D=20) where a dense BFGS Hessian
# (~160,000 entries) is both expensive and, per this session's own box-size diagnostic
# (docs/melitz_fixed_q_A_middle_loop_experiment_2026-07-30.md Phase 3), empirically prone to
# large, badly-scaled first steps unless the trust region/box is kept tight.
algorithm       1
eval_fcga       no
gradopt         exact
hessopt         6
feastol         1e-7
feastol_abs     1e-8
opttol          1e-3
opttol_abs      1e-4
outlev          1
honorbnds       always
